20 'WHEN COMPARING 'THE EXILES' AND  ''WE SHOULD STUDY FRIST THESIMILARITES OF CHARATORS, THEN PLOT AND FINALY THE THEMES.
30 PRINT"IN BRADBARY'S STORY THE CREW HAVE VIRGUELY NO PERSONSONLY.
40 PRINT"THEY ARE DESCRIBED AS CLEAN AND STERILE, LACKING ANY EMONITON OR HUMAN FEELING. IN SHORT A MR. SPOCK TYPE, WITHOUT VULCAN EARS. 
50 PRINT"ON THE OTHER HAND THE CREW IN THE 'CONSTANT READER', SEEM TO POSESS ENOUGH IDEOSINROUS AND NERROSES TO BE CONSIDERED NOT ONLY HUMAN, BUT ";
60 PRINT"ALSO ENOUGH THAT THEY CAN BE IDENIFIED AS PEOPLE. IN THIS SECOND SITUATION BOOKS ARE NOT RESTRICTED, JUST NEGLECTED.
70 PRINT"IT IS IN THIS FACT THAT THE COMPARISON OF THE CHARACTOR CAN BE MADE. 
80 PRINT"CLEAN MINDLESSNESS ON ONE HAND AND HUMAN DIFFERANCES ON THEOTHER.
90 PRINT"   WHEN CONSIDERING THE SIMILARITES AND DIFFERANCES OF THE TWO STORIES' PLOT, IT IS APPEREND THAT THE SIMILARITES ARE THE MOST OBVESOUS. IN BOTH STORIES A SHIP FROM EARTH IS SENT TO A PREVIOUSLY UNEXPLORED PLANET. 
100 PRINT"IN RESPONSE TO THIS INVASION THE PLANET ATTEMPS TO DEFEND   ITS SELF BY USING IDEAS FROM LITERATURE. THIS IS WERE THE SIMALARITES END AND THE DIFFERSECS EMERGE. FOR IN 'EXILES' THE ATTEMP IS FRUITLESS, WHILE A SIMILAR STRADIGY WORKS IN  ";
110 PRINT"'CONSTANT READER'.
